{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25890214",
      "title": "Adding a Data Model",
      "sourceHash": "5bed62023c153c2d203b22e7dfbe754ad153219f17dde0ad2dc1173921c74908",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.05,
          "end": 3.31,
          "en": "Now we got started",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.31,
          "end": 8.31,
          "en": "with our own components, with props, now let's refine this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 9.34,
          "end": 11.81,
          "en": "At the moment, a Todo is simply a string,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.81,
          "end": 15.01,
          "en": "and hence a list of Todos is an array of strings.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15.01,
          "end": 16.75,
          "en": "That could be what you need,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.75,
          "end": 19.34,
          "en": "but it would also not be unrealistic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.34,
          "end": 21.35,
          "en": "that every Todo is an object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.35,
          "end": 25.35,
          "en": "An object with an ID maybe, with a Todo text,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.35,
          "end": 27.46,
          "en": "maybe a title and a subtitle,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.46,
          "end": 30.05,
          "en": "and then maybe then also more metadata",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 30.05,
          "end": 33.08,
          "en": "that is attached to a Todo, like the author,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 33.08,
          "end": 35.23,
          "en": "the time when it was created,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 35.23,
          "end": 37.83,
          "en": "if it's currently active or not active?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 37.83,
          "end": 40.943,
          "en": "There are endless ways of describing a Todo.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 41.84,
          "end": 44.77,
          "en": "I don't wanna incorporate all those ways right now,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 44.77,
          "end": 48.18,
          "en": "but I definitely do want to refine it a little bit.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 48.18,
          "end": 49.013,
          "en": "And therefore,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 49.013,
          "end": 51.81,
          "en": "I'll add a new sub-folder in my source folder here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 51.81,
          "end": 54.24,
          "en": "which I'll name, models.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 54.24,
          "end": 55.9,
          "en": "You don't have to name it models,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 55.9,
          "end": 57.38,
          "en": "you can name it however you want,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 57.38,
          "end": 59.88,
          "en": "but I name it models because I want to describe",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 59.88,
          "end": 62.06,
          "en": "my different data models,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 62.06,
          "end": 66.28,
          "en": "my different kinds of data I'm working with in this project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 66.28,
          "end": 71.28,
          "en": "And in there, I'll add a todo.ts file, not .tsx, but .ts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 72.16,
          "end": 74.65,
          "en": "because I'm not creating a component in there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 74.65,
          "end": 77.76,
          "en": "It's also not in the components folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 77.76,
          "end": 80.1,
          "en": "And in this todo.ts file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 80.1,
          "end": 83.53999999999999,
          "en": "I want to describe how a Todo looks like.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 83.53999999999999,
          "end": 86.3,
          "en": "And for this, I wanna create my own Todo type.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 86.3,
          "end": 89.06,
          "en": "Now, we can do this with the type keyword,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 89.06,
          "end": 91.69,
          "en": "there also would be the interface keyword,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 91.69,
          "end": 94.47999999999999,
          "en": "which we can used as an alternative.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 94.47999999999999,
          "end": 98.443,
          "en": "Or we create a class, which we then even could instantiate.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 99.37,
          "end": 102.803,
          "en": "And I'll do the latter here, but either approach would work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 103.78999999999999,
          "end": 108.32,
          "en": "With that, I create a class Todo, and we create this class",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 108.32,
          "end": 112.61,
          "en": "basically just as we would do it in vanilla JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 112.61,
          "end": 115.47999999999999,
          "en": "Modern JavaScript has classes built in,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 115.47999999999999,
          "end": 117.67,
          "en": "and I'm just using that feature here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 117.67,
          "end": 120.56,
          "en": "It's also supported in TypeScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 120.56,
          "end": 124.28,
          "en": "And now here we can describe how our class should look like.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 124.28,
          "end": 126.75,
          "en": "And here we now got some slight differences",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 126.75,
          "end": 131.44,
          "en": "compared to how we do this in just JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 131.44,
          "end": 134.46,
          "en": "Because when working with TypeScript in classes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 134.46,
          "end": 137.01,
          "en": "if your class has different properties,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 137.01,
          "end": 139.8,
          "en": "different attributes, which you want to add,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 139.8,
          "end": 142.53,
          "en": "then you don't have to do this in the constructor,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 142.53,
          "end": 145.18,
          "en": "as you do it in vanilla JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 145.18,
          "end": 149.07,
          "en": "But instead you can add them directly here in the class",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 149.07,
          "end": 152.46,
          "en": "between the curly braces, as you're used to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 152.46,
          "end": 154.6,
          "en": "from some other programming languages,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 154.6,
          "end": 156.893,
          "en": "like C# for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 157.93,
          "end": 160.69,
          "en": "And here, I wanna make sure that a Todo object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 160.69,
          "end": 164.35,
          "en": "will always have an id and a text field for now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 164.35,
          "end": 167.03,
          "en": "And for this here, I'll add my id field",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 167.03,
          "end": 168.55,
          "en": "and then assign the type for that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 168.55,
          "end": 170.7,
          "en": "which will be string here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 170.7,
          "end": 172.21,
          "en": "And then I'll add my text field,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 172.21,
          "end": 174.46,
          "en": "which also will hold a string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 174.46,
          "end": 179.07,
          "en": "And then I'll export this Todo class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 179.07,
          "end": 181.03,
          "en": "And we're now getting some errors here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 181.03,
          "end": 183.43,
          "en": "regarding id and text.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 183.43,
          "end": 186.558,
          "en": "And we're seeing that the property text has no initializer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 186.558,
          "end": 190.38,
          "en": "and is not definitely assigned in the constructor.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 190.38,
          "end": 192.26,
          "en": "What this warning is telling us",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 192.26,
          "end": 194.44,
          "en": "is that I'm defining a class here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 194.44,
          "end": 196.87,
          "en": "which is meant to be instantiated,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 196.87,
          "end": 200.32,
          "en": "that's the main idea behind classes in general,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 200.32,
          "end": 202.19,
          "en": "but that those properties,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 202.19,
          "end": 206.5,
          "en": "which I set up and describe in there where I set the types,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 206.5,
          "end": 210.35,
          "en": "never receive a value, and we can make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 210.35,
          "end": 213.513,
          "en": "that they do receive a value by adding a constructor.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 214.48,
          "end": 219.48,
          "en": "This constructor could then also want some arguments",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 221.19,
          "end": 225.59,
          "en": "and here I want to get the todoText as an argument",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 225.59,
          "end": 228.28,
          "en": "because I'll generate the ID dynamically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 228.28,
          "end": 230.07,
          "en": "in the constructor then.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 230.07,
          "end": 233.07999999999998,
          "en": "And the todoText will also be of type string,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 233.07999999999998,
          "end": 235.76,
          "en": "hence the type annotation here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 235.76,
          "end": 239.73,
          "en": "So now we've got type annotations on the properties",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 239.73,
          "end": 243.37,
          "en": "and then here also on the constructor on the argument",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 243.37,
          "end": 245.7,
          "en": "And inside of the constructor,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 245.7,
          "end": 249.22,
          "en": "I'll then set this.text = todoText.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 249.22,
          "end": 251.55,
          "en": "Whoops, todoText here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 251.55,
          "end": 256.55,
          "en": "And I'll set this.id = an id which I want to generate here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 256.7,
          "end": 259.23,
          "en": "And I'll just use a Date() here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 259.23,
          "end": 262.1,
          "en": "and convert this to a string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 262.1,
          "end": 265.75,
          "en": "That's not a perfect unique ID, but it's good enough.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 265.75,
          "end": 268.83,
          "en": "So now whenever we create a new Todo,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 268.83,
          "end": 271.963,
          "en": "this ID gets created automatically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 273.36,
          "end": 277.02,
          "en": "And now we have this Todo object definition,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 277.02,
          "end": 281.35,
          "en": "this class definition here in this TypeScript file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 281.35,
          "end": 284.05,
          "en": "And that's very close to how this would look like",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 284.05,
          "end": 285.97,
          "en": "in just JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 285.97,
          "end": 288.45,
          "en": "In just JavaScript, we would basically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 288.45,
          "end": 291.11,
          "en": "not have these two property descriptions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 291.11,
          "end": 293.08,
          "en": "and we would just have this code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 293.08,
          "end": 296.90999999999997,
          "en": "which would work in just JavaScript, but in TypeScript,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 296.90999999999997,
          "end": 298.40999999999997,
          "en": "when using TypeScript,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 298.40999999999997,
          "end": 302.28,
          "en": "you also have to define those properties ahead of time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 302.28,
          "end": 304.66,
          "en": "to make it clear which types of values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 304.66,
          "end": 306.8,
          "en": "will be stored in there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 306.8,
          "end": 310.977,
          "en": "And with that, we can now use this Todo class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 310.977,
          "end": 314.43,
          "en": "And we can use it in app.tsx, for example",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 314.43,
          "end": 316.243,
          "en": "to create some dummy Todos.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 317.24,
          "end": 322.1,
          "en": "Here, we can have our Todos and that is an array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 322.1,
          "end": 324.99,
          "en": "and in that array, I want to now instantiate my Todos",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 324.99,
          "end": 327.5,
          "en": "based on this Todo class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 327.5,
          "end": 332.5,
          "en": "For this I'll import to do from ./models/todo.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 334,
          "end": 337.12,
          "en": "Again, you can omit the file extension here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 337.12,
          "end": 340.01,
          "en": "And then we instantiate and create those objects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 340.01,
          "end": 341.75,
          "en": "based on the Todo class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 341.75,
          "end": 344.473,
          "en": "just as we do it in vanilla JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 345.33,
          "end": 350.33,
          "en": "We can use new Todo() here, twice to create two Todos.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 351.9,
          "end": 354.52,
          "en": "And then we need to pass in that todoText,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 354.52,
          "end": 359.52,
          "en": "like Learn React and Learn TypeScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 360.68,
          "end": 362.9,
          "en": "And now our Todos, this here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 362.9,
          "end": 365.8,
          "en": "is no longer an array of strings,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 365.8,
          "end": 368.603,
          "en": "but instead an array of Todo objects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 369.9,
          "end": 372.57,
          "en": "Now I want to pass that as a value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 372.57,
          "end": 375,
          "en": "for the items prop into Todos.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 375,
          "end": 378.88,
          "en": "And to accept this array of Todo objects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 378.88,
          "end": 380.76,
          "en": "instead of array of strings",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 380.76,
          "end": 383.46,
          "en": "we have to change the type annotation here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 383.46,
          "end": 385.863,
          "en": "in the Todos component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 386.7,
          "end": 389.683,
          "en": "because there I currently want an array of strings.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 391.06,
          "end": 395.64,
          "en": "Now, the great thing is that if you are defining a class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 395.64,
          "end": 400.64,
          "en": "this class also acts not just as a constructor function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 401,
          "end": 404.37,
          "en": "which you can call to create new objects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 404.37,
          "end": 406.44,
          "en": "but also as a type.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 406.44,
          "end": 410.43,
          "en": "You can use your class name as a type.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 410.43,
          "end": 412.87,
          "en": "And therefore in the Todos component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 412.87,
          "end": 417.78,
          "en": "I can import Todo from going up one level,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 417.78,
          "end": 419.723,
          "en": "diving into models/todo,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 421.228,
          "end": 422.48,
          "en": "and we can make it clear",
